# Auto commit and push

After finishing work the user asked for, commit the relevant files and push to `origin` on the current branch. Do this by default. Do not ask first.

Skip only when the user says not to commit or push, or when the change is a secret (`.env`, credentials, keys).

Write a short commit message that says why the change exists. Never amend a commit that was already pushed. Never force-push to main.
